{"availability":"available","full":"xuedong-z/Fig-Draw","name":"Fig-Draw","description":"Browser-based post-processing editor for scientific figures — arrange panels, recolor from a 120-palette library, resize like figsize, and export publication-ready PNG/SVG. Runs entirely client-side.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":9,"forks":1,"created":"2026-05-31T16:14:36Z","updated":"2026-06-10T01:05:29Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://fig-draw.pages.dev","topics":["color-palettes","data-visualization","figure-editor","matplotlib","nextjs","publication","react","scientific-figures","svg-editor","typescript"],"demo":"https://fig-draw.pages.dev/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:20.217Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:20.217Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:20.217Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T08:58:20.217Z","stars":9,"forks":1}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A browser-based post-processing editor for scientific figures. Bring the SVGs you already exported from Origin, matplotlib, GraphPad Prism, etc. (and raster images like micrographs); SciCompose assembles them into one publication-ready figure — arrange panels, resize like figsize, recolor data series from a 120-palette library, refine single elements, unify type and line weights, and export a submission-grade PNG plus a re-editable SVG.","It runs entirely in your browser — no backend, no accounts, no AI, nothing leaves your machine. It is not a plotting tool; it post-processes figures you already made."],"features":["SVG figures — fully recognized & editable (axes, ticks, data, scatter, legend, text).","Raster images (PNG/JPG/WebP) — placed as image panels; scale (aspect-locked) and","Model-based resize (figsize) — drag a panel and the axes lengthen/shorten while","font size, line width, marker size, tick length, and label-to-axis distance stay constant, exactly like changing fig